    <string name="privacy_policy_title">"Privacy policy"</string>
    <string name="spoken_privacy">"Spoken summaries send refund totals to your device’s text-to-speech service, which may use the internet."</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_text">"Effective 15 November 2026.\n\nRefundavio helps you track purchases, returns, refunds, merchant follow-ups and warranties. You can use it without creating an account. The app stores the records and preferences you enter on your device. The app has no internet permission and contains no analytics or advertising SDK.\n\nWhen you attach a document, you choose it through your device’s document picker. Refundavio stores a reference to the document and keeps the file with its original provider. The provider and any app you use to open the document handle it under their own privacy policies.\n\nVoice shortcuts are optional. If you tap Speak, the speech recognition service on your device processes the audio and returns a transcript to Refundavio. If you enable spoken summaries, the device’s text-to-speech engine receives the text it reads, which can include refund totals. Those services may use the internet and follow their own privacy policies. You can type or select a shortcut and keep spoken summaries off.\n\nReminder notifications use generic text. When you copy a draft, Refundavio puts the selected text on your device’s clipboard so you can paste it into an app of your choice.\n\nYour purchase records stay on the device until you delete them. To remove those records and their refund and contact history, open More → Erase all purchase data. To remove preferences and all other app data, use your device’s app storage settings to clear Refundavio’s data, or uninstall it. Files you attached remain with their document provider.\n\nFor questions, contact the project through its GitHub issue tracker. Issues are public, so leave out receipts, order numbers, account details and other personal information. Refundavio support (https://github.com/lanray07/Refundavio/issues)"</string>
